From: harlan <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bmcweb: allow '-' in InsertMedia NFS image path and clarify message

validateImageUrl() (used for NFS image URLs) rejected any path containing a
dash, because '-' was missing from the allowed character class -- so ordinary
ISO names and FQDNs (e.g. openSUSE-Leap-15.6-...iso) failed with a confusing
ActionParameterValueFormatError.  Add '-' to the path regex, and rewrite the
journal message to name each allowed character unambiguously (forward slash,
backslash, underscore, period, dash) instead of bare glyphs.
---
 redfish-core/lib/virtual_media.hpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/redfish-core/lib/virtual_media.hpp
+++ b/redfish-core/lib/virtual_media.hpp
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@
     }
 
     // Regular expression to match the allowed characters
-    const std::regex pathPattern(R"(^[a-zA-Z0-9/_\\.]+$)");
+    const std::regex pathPattern(R"(^[a-zA-Z0-9/_\\.-]+$)");
 
     // Regular expression to validate FQDN
     const std::regex fqdnPattern(R"(^([a-zA-Z0-9-]{1,63}\.)+[a-zA-Z]{2,6}$)");
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@
     {
         std::cerr
             << "Error: Path = " << path
-            << "contains invalid characters. Allowed characters are alpha-numeric, '/', '\\', '_', and '.'."
+            << "contains invalid characters. Allowed characters are alpha-numeric, forward slash '/', backslash '\\', underscore '_', period '.', and dash '-'."
             << std::endl;
         return false;
     }
